{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1517663-the-true-apocalipse-in-wod","id":1517663,"title":"The True apocalipse in WOD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-10T16:50:28-07:00","id":1517663,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The True apocalipse in WOD","content":"I think it's even strange to talk about a &quot;true apocalypse&quot; in WOD considering that in the books several scenarios are offered for each game, however I believe that these stories all happen in the same passage of time in the same world and despite everything these events must collide at some point, I mean, one doesn't necessarily stop the other. What I mean is that if an apocalypse were to happen as a canonical event, what scenario(s) do you believe would happen and what would each kind of supernatural look like after all that. I can only think of the most tragic, but optimistic ending for this last one actually. Anyway, how do you think the world of WOD ended?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T21:07:28-07:00","id":1517737,"title":"","content":"I think the idea now is it ends when you want it to end in your chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T22:31:26-07:00","id":1517738,"title":"","content":"I'm well aware of this, usually when someone refers to the apocalypse in WOD it's usually because they want to end it all, even though I don't think it takes that much to end a chronicle, just to get closure for the characters if that's what they want.<br /> <br /> It could be taking over a city, defeating a Methuselah at his own game, getting rid of a curse, ending an age-old fight, defeating your biggest antagonist who could be Pentex, Technocracy or SI, or even ending a sect, a tribe or a tradition. At the end of the day, what I really want to know is what would be the most coherent ending, how people think WOD ended.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T12:06:22-07:00","id":1517802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1517663-the-true-apocalipse-in-wod?p=1517738#post1517738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm well aware of this, usually when someone refers to the apocalypse in WOD it's usually because they want to end it all, even though I don't think it takes that much to end a chronicle, just to get closure for the characters if that's what they want.<br /> <br /> It could be taking over a city, defeating a Methuselah at his own game, getting rid of a curse, ending an age-old fight, defeating your biggest antagonist who could be Pentex, Technocracy or SI, or even ending a sect, a tribe or a tradition. At the end of the day, what I really want to know is what would be the most coherent ending, how people think WOD ended.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;coherent&quot; for a supposed whole and singular WoD. Which can't even really happen in some ways, since you run into problems like Werewolf and Mage having mutually incompatible visions of the Umbra, or Demon saying &quot;Non-Dark Umbra? What's that?&quot;, or Demon not even really being wholly upfront about whether or not it's actually describing demons in a Biblical sense as interpreted through an almost entirely Christian lens, or if it's just the hosts filtering something that they can't fully grasp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T16:16:49-07:00","id":1517837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1517663-the-true-apocalipse-in-wod?p=1517802#post1517802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Define &quot;coherent&quot; for a supposed whole and singular WoD. Which can't even really happen in some ways, since you run into problems like Werewolf and Mage having mutually incompatible visions of the Umbra, or Demon saying &quot;Non-Dark Umbra? What's that?&quot;, or Demon not even really being wholly upfront about whether or not it's actually describing demons in a Biblical sense as interpreted through an almost entirely Christian lens, or if it's just the hosts filtering something that they can't fully grasp.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're okay with theories, let's start with a question, what's the difference between the Garou and Mages views of Umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T16:51:17-07:00","id":1517845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1517663-the-true-apocalipse-in-wod?p=1517837#post1517837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're okay with theories, let's start with a question, what's the difference between the Garou and Mages views of Umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>W:tA Umbra: Penumbra extends throughout the universe as a mirror of physical reality. The Deep Umbra refers to another, stranger place beyond a second Gauntlet that's kind of like physical reality in some ways, but way, way weirder.<br /> <br /> M:tAs Umbra: Penumbra is more of an Earth-local thing. The Deep Umbra is everything after the asteroid belt. Nothing beyond that is outside of the spirit world. The Horizon is also there, somewhere. Aliens are spirits and vice versa, depending on your point of view, never mind that the structure of the Umbra has some bits that don't change by vidare (you always need Entropy and Spirit to enter the Dark Umbra, even if you believe that any kind of Umbral travel is through &quot;the Underworld&quot;).<br /> <br /> Both fall out of basic assumptions of the games. In Mage, humans are the most important things in the universe and the structure of the Umbra pretty much has a limited physical reality around the Earth as a security blanket to humanity. In Werewolf, Gaia is the most important thing in the universe, and spans farther than human imagination can really reach, hence the fully physical universe with the Penumbra of the Middle Umbra as the soul of the world and the Deep Umbra as a reflection of what's really going on (Malfeas, the snarl where the Wyrm was trapped in the pattern web by the Weaver, is in the Deep Umbra rather than between it and the Penumbra as other &quot;Near Realms&quot; are).<br /> <br /> These two perspectives are not reconcilable. Mage is too tangled up even on its own terms to offer a means to it, though since M20, there have been efforts to try and build more bridges for crossover, such as with the &quot;Mythic Threads&quot; explanation for why disbelief kind of just bounces off Garou and Fera but can really mess up a Sphere effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T20:20:23-07:00","id":1517854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1517663-the-true-apocalipse-in-wod?p=1517845#post1517845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W:tA Umbra: Penumbra extends throughout the universe as a mirror of physical reality. The Deep Umbra refers to another, stranger place beyond a second Gauntlet that's kind of like physical reality in some ways, but way, way weirder.<br /> <br /> M:tAs Umbra: Penumbra is more of an Earth-local thing. The Deep Umbra is everything after the asteroid belt. Nothing beyond that is outside of the spirit world. The Horizon is also there, somewhere. Aliens are spirits and vice versa, depending on your point of view, never mind that the structure of the Umbra has some bits that don't change by vidare (you always need Entropy and Spirit to enter the Dark Umbra, even if you believe that any kind of Umbral travel is through &quot;the Underworld&quot;).<br /> <br /> Both fall out of basic assumptions of the games. In Mage, humans are the most important things in the universe and the structure of the Umbra pretty much has a limited physical reality around the Earth as a security blanket to humanity. In Werewolf, Gaia is the most important thing in the universe, and spans farther than human imagination can really reach, hence the fully physical universe with the Penumbra of the Middle Umbra as the soul of the world and the Deep Umbra as a reflection of what's really going on (Malfeas, the snarl where the Wyrm was trapped in the pattern web by the Weaver, is in the Deep Umbra rather than between it and the Penumbra as other &quot;Near Realms&quot; are).<br /> <br /> These two perspectives are not reconcilable. Mage is too tangled up even on its own terms to offer a means to it, though since M20, there have been efforts to try and build more bridges for crossover, such as with the &quot;Mythic Threads&quot; explanation for why disbelief kind of just bounces off Garou and Fera but can really mess up a Sphere effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you tell, how or why mages know or believe that the Umbra is... I don't know, a place in space, how a magician normally accesses the Umbra? I know Garou often use mirrors or reflective objects. By the way, there is a mention in one of the scenarios of the apocalypse (I think) that the Garou could intercept the red star, which opens the door for the Umbra to have a place as the mages suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T15:51:46-07:00","id":1517904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1517663-the-true-apocalipse-in-wod?p=1517854#post1517854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you tell, how or why mages know or believe that the Umbra is... I don't know, a place in space, how a magician normally accesses the Umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Different ways, and different ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know Garou often use mirrors or reflective objects. By the way, there is a mention in one of the scenarios of the apocalypse (I think) that the Garou could intercept the red star, which opens the door for the Umbra to have a place as the mages suppose. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you're saying, but there is a sidebar about how the Wyrm's forces will likely try to possess mages in the Last Battle scenario, to make sure that Garou do not trust them at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T05:53:45-07:00","id":1518027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1517663-the-true-apocalipse-in-wod?p=1517904#post1517904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what you're saying, but there is a sidebar about how the Wyrm's forces will likely try to possess mages in the Last Battle scenario, to make sure that Garou do not trust them at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention Entropy is still the dominion of the Wyrm and most of the Magi are familiar with it, uses it even... this most of the cases enough to register as &quot;Wyrm Tainted&quot; - sure ST choice, but the Garou more often than not treat anything remotely Wyrmish as enemies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T10:59:55-07:00","id":1518056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1517663-the-true-apocalipse-in-wod?p=1518027#post1518027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to mention Entropy is still the dominion of the Wyrm and most of the Magi are familiar with it, uses it even... this most of the cases enough to register as &quot;Wyrm Tainted&quot; - sure ST choice, but the Garou more often than not treat anything remotely Wyrmish as enemies</div> </div> </div> </div>A common misconception about using Sense Wyrm. Getting a result on the Gift is a red flag, not ultimate certainty of evil; unless it's accompanied by other red flags, it's more often a call for covertly purifying someone or something. Now, it is true that Garou and no small number of Fera would probably consider the Special K to be another red flag worthy of a summary execution if the subject is also carrying around taint, the Philodox and Theurge auspices together are supposed to have deeper thinkers that consider broader scenarios than just &quot;the mage is clearly guilty because of this kegare-alike we found on them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T16:00:15-07:00","id":1518095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1517663-the-true-apocalipse-in-wod?p=1518056#post1518056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A common misconception about using Sense Wyrm. Getting a result on the Gift is a red flag, not ultimate certainty of evil; unless it's accompanied by other red flags, it's more often a call for covertly purifying someone or something. Now, it is true that Garou and no small number of Fera would probably consider the Special K to be another red flag worthy of a summary execution if the subject is also carrying around taint, the Philodox and Theurge auspices together are supposed to have deeper thinkers that consider broader scenarios than just &quot;the mage is clearly guilty because of this kegare-alike we found on them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I am deeply amused by you telling this to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T14:02:20-07:00","id":1518376,"title":"","content":"I kind of run a single coherent world when I do run games and generally I have all of the Apocalypse scenarios going at the same time and the players get to decide which ones they work on if their characters actually become powerful enough to matter to an apocalypse scenario","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T19:19:31-07:00","id":1518400,"title":"","content":"If I was going to do a coherent singular apocalypse for a long-running campaign, it'd probably have to be one that is entirely homebrew. I don't use any of the metaplot at all. It's just declared non-canon at my game table. In other words, if you play in a game I'm ST'ing, assume that WoD5 and most of Revised just flat out didn't happen at all. It's a lot closer to the 2e version of WoD in all its gonzo glory, with some of the hindsight from the X20 lines thrown in. Yeah, I'm a sucker for Classic 90's WoD and I liked how V20 had that perfect balance of being a metaplot-agnostic toolkit.<br /> <br /> BUT if I were to run an apocalyptic event, then there's nothing that says I couldn't crib elements from the various Time of Judgment books that I do like.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire</b> will probably require a custom scenario that's not in the Gehenna book at all, but maybe it can borrow a few specific moments from each of the scenarios like the Shaper (or any other &quot;Caitiff Antediluvian&quot; who never sired) or the Gangrel Antediluvian trying to meld with the Earth.<br /> <br /> With <b>Werewolf</b>, I'd go with a mix between A Tribe Falls and my own custom scenario ideas that involve one last grand battle against the Wyrm and the Weaver. The entirety of the Gaian Fera finally reunite and put aside their differences for the very last battle. The Triat is defeated (even the Wyld falls in the chaos of battle) but Gaia is alive and on top. All Fera go extinct but the souls of the Gaian Garou are reincarnated in the Summer Country of the Umbra, forever protected and cared for by Gaia.<br /> <br /> Now, <b>Mage</b> is the most straightforward of the main three. I'd just use the Judgment scenario from the Ascension book with only a few minor tweaks.<br /> <br /> When we get into the other gamelines and the Time of Judgment book, then it gets a little tricky....<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling</b>: I'm just gonna go with a variant of <i>Starlight Exodus</i>. The Kithain and all the other Fae all retreat to the Dreaming at the same time all of humanity awakens during the events of Judgment. Mage and Changeling get their scenarios happening simultaneously and they also happen to be the very last ones to happen.<br /> <br /> <b>Kindred of the East: </b>I'm gonna be honest, I never liked KOTE all that much. Or at least not the Kuei-Jin in and of themselves. There's a lot of elements within the line I liked but retconning the Kuei-Jin was probably the one good call V5 actually made. I'm not even going to comment on the unfortunate levels of Orientalism within the game as a whole.<br /> <br /> But if I had to pick a scenario to &quot;canonize&quot;, I'm gonna go with <i>The Trumpet of Mount Meru</i> and have a similar scenario not only apply to the Shih, but also Strike Force Zero and all of the Western hunter groups such as the Society of Leopold, the FBI Special Affairs Department, the Arcanum, the Orphic Circle, et cetera. Hell, I'd even allow the less prominent mortal hunter groups like the Young Bloods MC or the Mafia be eligible for these grand endowments of power. Basically, all these mortal hunter groups get what can best be described as &quot;Numina on Steroids, Meth, and PCP&quot;, flip the fuck out, and start hunting down every single Kindred, Risen, Fera (be it Gaian or Wyrmish), Demon, Mage, Mummy, what have you.<br /> <br /> This would be the very first scenario to kick off the Time of Judgment and every single event would follow from that.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter: </b>I liked Hunter: The Reckoning and even got to play a one-shot of it a couple of years ago, but Imbued only make sense with the Sixth Great Maelstrom taken into account with the rest of the WoD setting. Unlike the original five WoD games, Reckoning is tied with the metaplot from the very get-go. Just stick to Hunters Hunted and the other Mortals books and invoke the reimagined &quot;Trumpet of Mount Meru&quot; scenario, though if you do want the Imbued thrown in the mix, have that same event give all Imbued five-dot Edges and maximum Conviction as part of the last battles, joining the more organized hunters in battle. I could cook up an alternate HTR that doesn't involve the Sixth Great Maelstrom but that's gonna be on the backburner for a while.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy: </b>Never played Mummy nor read it, so I can't comment.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon: </b>I have read Demon, have not played it, and I don't really want to. Much like how the Kuei-Jin are kind of squicky with their Orientalism, Demon is very squicky on a religious level and this applies to damn near every religion past or present once you factor in the infamous Earthbound book. Even when you account for the more revisionist Milton-esque view of Lucifer presented in Demon, I still ain't touching that shit with a ten foot pole so I am just gonna move on...<br /> <br /> <b>Wraith: </b>I don't know much about Wraith, have never played it, but unlike Demon, Reckoning, or Mummy, I'd like to actually try it out one day and the concept itself is interesting. I've never read <i>Ends of Empire</i> but I do know that it's the book that kicks off the Sixth Great Maelstrom which gives us Demon: The Fallen and Hunter: The Reckoning. Once I get a better feel for Wraith and learn more about its setting, I'll give Ends of Empire a look and see if I can cook up a modified version of <i>Ends of Empire</i> or an entirely new scenario altogether.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":".  Edited for clarity and conciseness 07-20-2023, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}